-- `dropout` draws its mask from a key, so a function that drops out takes a
-- `key` parameter, as an initializer does. Without one the mask would come
-- from a hidden stream, and the backward pass — which recomputes the
-- forward — would get a different mask and therefore a wrong gradient.
dim B

fn bad(x : ℝ[batch: B, model: 4]) -> ℝ[batch: B, model: 4] uses Rand =
  dropout(0.2, 0.5, x)
